  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an odd integer NNN and two integer sequences A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ and B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.\n\nYour task is to reorder the elements of BBB, forming a new sequence C1,C2,…,CNC_1, C_2, \\ldots, C_NC1​,C2​,…,CN​ (i.e. choose a permutation P1,P2,…,PNP_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​ of the integers 111 through NNN, where Ci=BPiC_i = B_{P_i}Ci​=BPi​​ for each valid iii), in such a way that the following condition holds: (A1⊕C1)=(A2⊕C2)=…=(AN⊕CN)(A_1 \\oplus C_1) = (A_2 \\oplus C_2) = \\ldots = (A_N \\oplus C_N)(A1​⊕C1​)=(A2​⊕C2​)=…=(AN​⊕CN​), where ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes bitwise XOR. Find one such reordered sequence or determine that it is impossible.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\le N \\le 10^51≤N≤105",
      "NNN is odd",
      "0≤Ai≤1060 \\le A_i \\le 10^60≤Ai​≤106 for each valid iii",
      "0≤Bi≤1060 \\le B_i \\le 10^60≤Bi​≤106 for each valid iii"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case:\n\n\nIf there is no valid way to reorder the sequence BBB, print a single line containing the integer −1-1−1.\nOtherwise, print a single line containing NNN space-separated integers C1,C2,…,CNC_1, C_2, \\ldots, C_NC1​,C2​,…,CN​. If there are multiple solutions, you may find any one.",
    "notes": [],
